  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Aiko Aiko** (1 review): The reviewer found the show's opening Iko Iko wonderful [2]\n- **Althea** (1 review): Reviewer says Mayer has called Althea his favorite song to play, and it shone here, especially in the Eyes>Althea run [4]\n- **Morning Dew** (1 review): The reviewer felt Morning Dew closed the main show with a smoking performance [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Aiko Aiko**: back after 53 archived shows (681 days); rare: 12 archived performances [5]\n- **Drums/Space/Jam**: rare: 3 archived performances [5]\n- **Johnny B. Goode**: rare: 13 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **dac2018-06-08.AKGmix.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 17 songs; 168 min; rated 4.33/5 by 3 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The venue has had several names: Coca-Cola Lakewood, Aarons Amphitheater, and now Cellairis Amphitheater at Lakewood, which even longtime locals didn't recognize [3]\n- Reviewer's second Dead & Company show after Cincinnati earlier that week; Mayer raised his energy playing in his musical hometown [4]\n- Uploader saw only the name Lakewood at the venue, no Cellairis Amphitheater signage, and wondered whether the name had changed again [1]\n- Unlike 2015 and early Dead & Company shows criticized for slow tempos, this show's pacing felt right to the reviewer [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **dac2018-06-08.AKGmix.flac16**: taped by Toaste; transferred by Toaste; source: DFC lawn, stand at about 10 feet > 2x AKG 391 cardioids ORTF and 2x AKG 393 hypercardioids pointed at stacks > Zoom F8 @44.1kHz/16-bit (4-track) > .wav > SDXC [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by Live Music Blog: [SETLIST / TWEETS: Dead and Company @ Cellairis Amphitheatre at Lakewood, Atlanta GA 6.8.18 - Live Music Blog](https://livemusicblog.com/setlist-dead-and-company-atlanta/) [6]",
